#!/bin/sh
# S298's guest: PID 1 on the lane VM's kernel. Runs the patched bash on the
# command and on the trap's command, then a uprobe on Alpine's stock bash,
# prints what the driver printed between markers, and powers off.
export PATH=/bin:/usr/bin
mount -t devtmpfs dev /dev
mount -t proc proc /proc
mount -t sysfs sys /sys
mount -t tmpfs tmp /tmp
ln -s /proc/self/fd /dev/fd
printf 'echo "$1"\n' > /tmp/src.sh
echo "=== run signal main"
timeout 300 drive signal /bin/bash-pt /cmd.sh 2>&1
echo "=== run signal trap"
timeout 60 drive signal /bin/bash-pt /cmd-trap.sh 2>&1
echo "=== run uprobe main"
timeout 300 drive uprobe /bin/bash /cmd.sh 2>&1
echo "=== end"
poweroff -f
